            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_1",
            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Nguyen Van Cu",
            "review_text": "Duc L\n1 contribution\n0\nWorst experience ever\nJan 2025 • Family\nI heard of this restaurant from a friend as one of the best “broken rice” restaurants in Saigon, so I decided to give it a try despite the fact that my cousin living in Nam told me not to because I want to “experience” it. \nThe restaurant is tiny. So even though they use the “shared tables” model, they can only sit roughly 30 people at max capacity. The room has no AC so they turn on a few fans which blow the smoke from the grill straight to your face. When I left the restaurant, my whole body smells like one freaking walking pork chop. \nThey sat my cousin and I with another strange couple in a 4-seat table. After starring at each other for 10 mins and the food still didn’t come out, that couple couldn’t take it anymore so they just got up and left. It took more than 30 mins for the food to finally come out and still no drinks. I looked around and everyone looked so tense because of the heat, the smoke and constant yelling from the waiters & waitresses. They argued with each other loudly and didn’t give a fudge about the customers. \nI ate about half of my portion and couldn’t take it anymore so I decided I had enough of an “experience” and just paid and left. It’s a lot more expensive compares to the other restaurants serving the same dish. \nSave yourself money and time. You’re on vacation and should have a pleasant time especially while eating. Don’t make the same mistake as I did.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 13, 2025",
