            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Nguyen Van Cu",
            "review_text": "KiKi\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam26 contributions\n0\nGood broken rice with pork chop\nJul 2024 • Family\nThis restaurant has been famous in Saigon for decades, so I decided to give it a try. My friend and I ordered the pork chop with pork pie and shredded pork skin, and a bowl of veggie soup. The prices here are on the higher side compared to other places, with just the pork chop dish costing 170vnd and the soup 50vnd.\n\nThe pork chop was too huge to me, and the shredded pork skin was thinly sliced, with thick slices of meat beautifully arranged on top. Pork pie is not good, i dont like it. The pork chop was marinated well, and the fish sauce that came with it was perfectly balanced. The soup was hearty, with lots of vegetables and tender ribs, and it tasted okay.\n\nHowever, the space was quite hot and smoky, and the food took a long time to arrive even though the restaurant wasn’t busy. When I ordered a takeaway portion, they didn’t include pickled vegetables, only fish sauce, which was a bit disappointing.\nRead more\nWritten August 13, 2024",
