            "review_text": "Lili T\nSydney, Australia4 contributions\n0\nMs Ngoc\nFeb 2020 • Solo\nOne of the best com tam I'd tried in Saigon, with soft and tender pork chop, very soft and moist rice, chã is one the best I tried so far and sauces is well taste.\n\nPricing at 140k dong ($9 aud), for pork chop with chã and rice relatively expensive for Vietnamese people. However beware of the pricing charge, no menu with price on it (no transparent), offering tea but might include in the charges, even customers don't drink or ask for it. Like many restaurant in Saigon, restaurant leave wet wipe on the table and when customers don't use it they still get charges, which I found very shifty. I happy to provide tips but dishonest business should be prohibited!\n\nThree star rating for the food but no star for service and no star for the pricing transparency.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 5, 2020",
